  "result": "I'm wrapping up. I searched the archive several ways and found no ticket that matches this problem.\n\n{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I couldn't find an earlier report of Command Palette blocking the \\\"|\\\" key, including the pattern where it only types in elevated apps. Two tickets look similar but aren't the same problem. PowerToys#47617 and PowerToys#47491 are about \\\"|\\\" on French AZERTY keyboards launching Text Extractor or screen capture. The cause there was another module's shortcut, and in PowerToys#47491 turning off ZoomIt fixed it. Your report points at Command Palette instead, because turning it off fixes the problem and turning off its extensions doesn't. Please file this as a new bug. Include the key combination you use for \\\"|\\\" and your keyboard layout, and say whether the Command Palette hotkey or any alias is set to something unusual. Also attach a PowerToys bug report ZIP. In the meantime, you can turn Command Palette off, or run the affected apps as administrator.\"}",
